{"seed":{"mim":"620507","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"ICHTHYOSIS WITH ERYTHROKERATODERMA","alt_titles":[],"symbol":"IEKD","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2023},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"ICHTHYOSIS WITH ERYTHROKERATODERMA","mim":"620507","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:37212630","type":"Paper","label":"Takeichi et al. (2023)","pmid":"37212630","year":2023,"content_level":"title","relevance":"primary","title":"KLK11 ichthyosis: large truncal hyperkeratotic pigmented plaques underscore a distinct autosomal dominant disorder of cornification."},{"id":"paper:36689511","type":"Paper","label":"Gong et al. (2023)","pmid":"36689511","year":2023,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Variants in KLK11, affecting signal peptide cleavage of kallikrein-related peptidase 11, cause an autosomal-dominant cornification disorder."},{"id":"finding:36689511:1","type":"Finding","label":"Gong et al. (2023) described a previously undescribed autosomal dominant cornification disorder in 1 familial case and 2 sporadic cases. The disorder was characterized by early-onset ichthyosiform erythroderma or erythrokeratoderma. Patients' skin showed a thickened, dense stratum corneum, which the authors took as a sign of abnormal desquamation.","pmid":"36689511","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"gene:KLK11","type":"Gene","label":"KLK11"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001019","type":"Phenotype","label":"Erythroderma","hpo_id":"HP:0001019"},{"id":"phenotext:erythrokeratoderma","type":"PhenotypeText","label":"erythrokeratoderma"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000962","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hyperkeratosis","hpo_id":"HP:0000962"},{"id":"inh:AD","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal dominant","hpo_id":"HP:0000006"},{"id":"finding:36689511:2","type":"Finding","label":"Whole-exome sequencing in 3 families (1 familial case and 2 sporadic cases) was used by Gong et al. (2023) to find 2 heterozygous variants affecting Gly50 in KLK11. These variants lie around the signal peptide cleavage site. One of them was c.149G>A (p.Gly50Glu). In overexpression systems, the variants disrupted signal peptide cleavage of KLK11. The Gly50Glu variant caused subcellular mislocalization and reduced extracellular secretion.","pmid":"36689511","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:KLK11:c.149G>A","type":"Variant","label":"KLK11 c.149G>A / p.G50E","gene":"KLK11","keys":["c.149G>A","p.G50E"],"omim_name":"KLK11, GLY50GLU"},{"id":"finding:36689511:3","type":"Finding","label":"Gong et al. (2023) found significantly lower trypsin-like and chymotrypsin-like proteolytic activity in patients' stratum corneum. They also found reduced proteolysis of desmoglein-1 and delayed breakdown of corneodesmosomes, which pointed to delayed skin desquamation.","pmid":"36689511","section":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"gene:DSG1","type":"Gene","label":"DSG1"},{"id":"finding:36689511:4","type":"Finding","label":"Gong et al. (2023) made mice homozygous for the Klk11 variant c.131G>A (p.Gly44Glu), the equivalent of human KLK11 p.Gly50Glu. These mice had hyperkeratosis and abnormal desquamation, partly reproducing the human phenotype.","pmid":"36689511","section":"animal_model"},{"id":"variant:KLK11:c.131G>A","type":"Variant","label":"KLK11 c.131G>A / p.G44E","gene":"KLK11","keys":["c.131G>A","p.G44E"],"omim_name":"KLK11, GLY44GLU"},{"id":"finding:37212630:1","type":"Finding","label":"Takeichi et al. (2023) reported KLK11 ichthyosis with large hyperkeratotic pigmented plaques on the trunk. They described it as a distinct autosomal dominant disorder of cornification.","pmid":"37212630","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0008064","type":"Phenotype","label":"Ichthyosis","hpo_id":"HP:0008064"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0200035","type":"Phenotype","label":"Skin plaque","hpo_id":"HP:0200035"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000953","type":"Phenotype","label":"Hyperpigmentation of the skin","hpo_id":"HP:0000953"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:36689511","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:36689511:1"},{"src":"finding:36689511:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:36689511:1","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:KLK11","pmid":"36689511"},{"src":"finding:36689511:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0001019","pmid":"36689511","present":true,"text":"early-onset ichthyosiform erythroderma"},{"src":"finding:36689511:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"phenotext:erythrokeratoderma","pmid":"36689511","pres